---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Electricity Bill Calculator India – Monthly Unit & Appliance Cost Calculator"
  description="Calculate your monthly electricity bill in India based on units consumed (kWh), state-wise tariff rates, slab billing, and appliance-wise power consumption."
  category="General"
  calculatorName="Electricity Bill Calculator"
  slug="electricity-bill-calculator"
  keywords={[
    'electricity bill calculator',
    'electricity bill calculator india',
    'electricity unit calculator',
    'electricity cost calculator',
    'units to bill calculator',
    'electricity bill per unit',
    'electricity consumption calculator',
    'power bill calculator',
    'light bill calculator'
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">

    <!-- TABS -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-2.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 overflow-x-auto pb-1 text-xs font-semibold scrollbar-thin">
        <button type="button" class="btn-elec-tab active shrink-0 rounded-lg bg-yellow-500 px-3.5 py-1.5 font-bold text-white shadow-xs cursor-pointer" data-tab="units">By Units Consumed (kWh)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-elec-tab shrink-0 rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3.5 py-1.5 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-tab="appliance">By Appliance Usage 🏠</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-elec-tab shrink-0 rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3.5 py-1.5 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-tab="state">State-wise Rates ⚡</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PRESETS -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-3.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-xs">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mr-1">⚡ Quick States:</span>
        <button type="button" class="btn-state-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-yellow-500 hover:text-yellow-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-rate="6.50" data-state="Delhi">🏛️ Delhi (₹6.50/unit)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-state-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-yellow-500 hover:text-yellow-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-rate="7.50" data-state="Maharashtra">🏙️ Maharashtra (₹7.50/unit)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-state-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-yellow-500 hover:text-yellow-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-rate="5.80" data-state="UP">🌾 Uttar Pradesh (₹5.80/unit)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-state-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-yellow-500 hover:text-yellow-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-rate="7.80" data-state="Karnataka">🌿 Karnataka (₹7.80/unit)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-state-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-yellow-500 hover:text-yellow-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-rate="6.00" data-state="Gujarat">🏭 Gujarat (₹6.00/unit)</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- MAIN PANEL -->
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-yellow-50/20 to-amber-50/20 p-5 shadow-xl shadow-slate-900/5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-950 dark:to-yellow-950/10 sm:p-7">

      <!-- UNITS PANEL -->
      <div id="panel-units" class="elec-panel space-y-5">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
          <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2"><span>⚡</span> Electricity Bill Calculator by Units</h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Enter total units consumed from your meter reading and your state's electricity tariff rate to calculate your monthly bill.</p>
        </div>
        <form id="form-elec-units" class="space-y-4" novalidate onsubmit="return false;">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div><label for="elec-units" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Units Consumed (kWh)</label><input type="number" id="elec-units" value="200" step="1" min="0" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" /></div>
            <div><label for="elec-rate" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Rate per Unit (₹/kWh)</label><input type="number" id="elec-rate" value="6.50" step="0.1" min="0" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" /></div>
            <div><label for="elec-fixed" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Fixed / Demand Charge (₹/month)</label><input type="number" id="elec-fixed" value="100" step="10" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" /></div>
            <div><label for="elec-tax" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Electricity Duty / Tax (%)</label><input type="number" id="elec-tax" value="5" step="1" min="0" max="30" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" /></div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 pt-2">
            <button type="submit" id="btn-elec-calc" class="flex-1 rounded-xl bg-yellow-500 hover:bg-yellow-600 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-yellow-500/25 transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer">Calculate Electricity Bill →</button>
            <button type="button" id="btn-elec-clear" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 transition cursor-pointer">Clear (✕)</button>
          </div>
        </form>
      </div>

      <!-- APPLIANCE PANEL -->
      <div id="panel-appliance" class="elec-panel hidden space-y-5">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
          <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2"><span>🏠</span> Appliance-wise Electricity Consumption</h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Select your appliances and daily usage to estimate monthly electricity consumption and cost.</p>
        </div>
        <form id="form-appliance" class="space-y-4" novalidate onsubmit="return false;">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-2 text-xs">
            <!-- Appliance rows -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-2 p-2 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 font-bold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
              <span>Appliance</span><span class="text-center">Watts</span><span class="text-center">Qty</span><span class="text-center">Hours/Day</span>
            </div>
            <div id="appliance-rows" class="space-y-1.5"></div>
          </div>
          <div><label class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Your Rate (₹/unit)</label><input type="number" id="app-rate" value="6.50" step="0.1" class="mt-1.5 w-40 rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" /></div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <button type="submit" id="btn-app-calc" class="flex-1 rounded-xl bg-yellow-500 hover:bg-yellow-600 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-yellow-500/25 transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer">Calculate Appliance Cost →</button>
            <button type="button" id="btn-app-clear" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 transition cursor-pointer">Clear (✕)</button>
          </div>
        </form>
      </div>

      <!-- STATE RATES PANEL -->
      <div id="panel-state" class="elec-panel hidden space-y-5">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
          <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2"><span>🗺️</span> State-wise Electricity Rates in India (2025)</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
            <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
              <tr><th class="p-2.5">State</th><th class="p-2.5 text-right">Avg Rate (₹/unit)</th><th class="p-2.5 text-right">Fixed Charge</th><th class="p-2.5">DISCOM</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800 font-mono">
              <tr><td class="p-2.5 font-bold">Delhi</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹3.00 – ₹8.00</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹125/month</td><td class="p-2.5 text-slate-500">BSES/TPDDL</td></tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/30"><td class="p-2.5 font-bold">Maharashtra</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹3.95 – ₹11.45</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹130/month</td><td class="p-2.5 text-slate-500">MSEDCL</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-2.5 font-bold">Karnataka</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹4.90 – ₹8.20</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹60/month</td><td class="p-2.5 text-slate-500">BESCOM</td></tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/30"><td class="p-2.5 font-bold">Gujarat</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹3.35 – ₹6.95</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹60/month</td><td class="p-2.5 text-slate-500">DGVCL/UGVCL</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-2.5 font-bold">Uttar Pradesh</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹3.00 – ₹7.00</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹110/month</td><td class="p-2.5 text-slate-500">PVVNL/UPPCL</td></tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/30"><td class="p-2.5 font-bold">Tamil Nadu</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹0 – ₹7.00 (1st 100 free)</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹50/month</td><td class="p-2.5 text-slate-500">TANGEDCO</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-2.5 font-bold">Rajasthan</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹3.75 – ₹8.25</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹100/month</td><td class="p-2.5 text-slate-500">JVVNL/AVVNL</td></tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/30"><td class="p-2.5 font-bold">West Bengal</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹5.50 – ₹9.00</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹75/month</td><td class="p-2.5 text-slate-500">CESC/WBSEDCL</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-2.5 font-bold">Madhya Pradesh</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹3.60 – ₹7.20</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹80/month</td><td class="p-2.5 text-slate-500">MPEZ/MPMKVVCL</td></tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/30"><td class="p-2.5 font-bold">Punjab</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹2.00 – ₹8.22</td><td class="p-2.5 text-right">₹65/month</td><td class="p-2.5 text-slate-500">PSPCL</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">*Rates are approximate averages for domestic consumers (2025). Slab-based tariffs apply in most states. Check your DISCOM website for exact rates.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- RESULTS -->
      <div id="elec-results" class="hidden mt-6 space-y-5">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-yellow-200 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-yellow-50/40 to-amber-100/50 p-5 shadow-lg shadow-yellow-500/5 dark:border-yellow-900/60 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-900 dark:to-yellow-950/30 sm:p-7">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4 border-b border-yellow-200/80 pb-4 dark:border-slate-800">
            <div>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-yellow-700 dark:text-yellow-300">⚡ Total Monthly Bill</span>
              <div id="elec-res-total" class="mt-1 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-yellow-600 dark:text-yellow-400">₹1,430</div>
            </div>
            <div class="sm:text-right">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">Annual Electricity Cost:</span>
              <div id="elec-res-annual" class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white">₹17,160/year</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 text-xs">
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-yellow-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 font-semibold">Units Consumed</div>
              <div id="elec-res-units" class="mt-1 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">200 kWh</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-yellow-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 font-semibold">Energy Charge</div>
              <div id="elec-res-energy" class="mt-1 text-sm font-bold text-yellow-600 dark:text-yellow-400">₹1,300</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-yellow-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 font-semibold">Fixed + Tax</div>
              <div id="elec-res-fixed" class="mt-1 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">₹130</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-yellow-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 font-semibold">Cost per Day</div>
              <div id="elec-res-per-day" class="mt-1 text-sm font-bold text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">₹47.67/day</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SEO CONTENT -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <section class="elec-content">
      <h2>Electricity Bill Calculator India – Monthly Cost & Unit Calculator</h2>
      <p>Our <strong>Electricity Bill Calculator</strong> is designed specifically for Indian households to calculate their monthly electricity bill accurately. Simply enter your meter reading (units consumed in kWh), your state's electricity tariff rate, fixed charges, and any applicable electricity duty to get your exact monthly electricity bill — no manual calculation needed.</p>

      <h2>How Is Your Electricity Bill Calculated in India?</h2>
      <p>Your monthly electricity bill in India typically consists of:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Energy Charge:</strong> Units consumed × Rate per unit. This is the main component of your bill and varies by consumption slab.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed / Demand Charge:</strong> A fixed monthly charge regardless of consumption — typically ₹50–₹150/month based on your sanctioned load (in kW).</li>
        <li><strong>Electricity Duty:</strong> State tax on energy charges, usually 5%–15% of the energy charge.</li>
        <li><strong>Fuel Adjustment Charge (FAC):</strong> Variable charge adjusted quarterly based on fuel costs.</li>
        <li><strong>Meter Rent:</strong> Small monthly charge for the electricity meter (~₹10–₹30/month in most states).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Understanding Slab-Based Tariffs</h2>
      <p>Most Indian state electricity boards use a <strong>slab-based tariff system</strong> where higher consumption is charged at progressively higher rates:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Slab 1 (0–100 units):</strong> Lowest rate (e.g., ₹3.00/unit in Delhi)</li>
        <li><strong>Slab 2 (101–200 units):</strong> Medium rate (e.g., ₹4.50/unit)</li>
        <li><strong>Slab 3 (201–400 units):</strong> Higher rate (e.g., ₹6.00/unit)</li>
        <li><strong>Slab 4 (400+ units):</strong> Highest rate (e.g., ₹7.50–₹8.00/unit)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This means consuming 210 units is significantly more expensive than 199 units — because the 200 units cross into the higher slab for all units in that tier (in many states).</p>

      <h2>Average Electricity Consumption by Appliance (Indian Homes)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>1-Ton AC (5-star):</strong> ~1000W, 8 hrs/day = 8 units/day = 240 units/month</li>
        <li><strong>Refrigerator (250L, 5-star):</strong> ~0.80 units/day = 24 units/month</li>
        <li><strong>Washing Machine (Automatic, 6kg):</strong> ~1.5 units/wash, 15 washes/month = 22.5 units</li>
        <li><strong>LED TV (40-inch):</strong> ~0.05 units/hr, 6 hrs/day = 9 units/month</li>
        <li><strong>Ceiling Fan (5-star):</strong> ~35W, 10 hrs/day = 0.35 units/day = 10.5 units/month</li>
        <li><strong>Geyser (15L):</strong> ~2 units per use. Major contributor to winter bills!</li>
        <li><strong>LED Bulbs (10W × 5 lights):</strong> ~0.05 units/hr × 8 hrs = 0.4 units/day = 12 units/month</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Tips to Reduce Your Electricity Bill in India</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Switch to 5-Star Rated Appliances:</strong> 5-star ACs, refrigerators, and washing machines consume 20%–40% less electricity than 1-star models.</li>
        <li><strong>Use AC Smartly:</strong> Set AC to 24°C–26°C instead of 18°C. Each degree lower increases consumption by ~3%–5%.</li>
        <li><strong>Use Solar Panels:</strong> Rooftop solar under PM Surya Ghar Muft Bijli Yojana provides up to 300 free units/month and subsidizes installation.</li>
        <li><strong>Off-peak Usage:</strong> Run heavy appliances (washing machine, dishwasher) during off-peak hours if your state offers Time-of-Day (ToD) tariffs.</li>
        <li><strong>Fix Power Factor:</strong> For homes with many motors/compressors, install a capacitor bank to improve power factor and reduce reactive charges.</li>
        <li><strong>Smart Meters:</strong> Request a smart meter installation — they help track real-time consumption and identify energy-wasting appliances.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>State-wise Electricity Rates in India</h2>
      <p>Electricity rates vary significantly across Indian states. As of 2025, the average domestic tariff ranges from approximately ₹3.50/unit (Tamil Nadu first slab) to over ₹9.00/unit (higher slabs in Maharashtra and West Bengal). Southern states generally have lower base rates, while metro cities tend to have higher fixed charges but more subsidized slabs for low-consumption households.</p>
    </section>
  </Fragment>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <Fragment slot="faq">
    <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800" open>
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none"><h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">1. How do I read my electricity meter in India?<span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span></h3></summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Read the 5-digit number displayed on your meter dial or digital display. Subtract last month's reading from this month's reading to get units consumed. One unit = 1 kilowatt-hour (kWh) = using 1000 watts for 1 hour.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none"><h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">2. What is 1 unit of electricity in India?<span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span></h3></summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">1 unit of electricity = 1 kilowatt-hour (kWh). This means running a 1000W appliance (like a large AC or geyser) for 1 hour consumes 1 unit. A 100W fan running for 10 hours also consumes 1 unit.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none"><h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">3. What is the electricity rate in Delhi?<span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span></h3></summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Delhi uses slab-based tariff: 0–200 units at ₹3.00–₹4.50/unit; 201–400 units at ₹6.50/unit; 400+ units at ₹8.00/unit. First 200 units are subsidized for households consuming below 400 units/month. Fixed charge is ₹125/month.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none"><h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">4. Which appliance consumes the most electricity?<span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span></h3></summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Air conditioners are the biggest electricity consumers in Indian homes, followed by geysers (water heaters) in winter. A 1.5-ton AC running 8 hours/day consumes approximately 350–400 units/month. Geysers consume 2–3 units per use.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none"><h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">5. How can I get free electricity in India?<span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span></h3></summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">The PM Surya Ghar Muft Bijli Yojana provides up to 300 units of free electricity per month to households that install rooftop solar panels. The government provides subsidies of ₹30,000–₹78,000 on installation costs. Additionally, several states offer free electricity to below-poverty-line (BPL) families.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none"><h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">6. What is electricity duty in India?<span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span></h3></summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Electricity duty is a state tax levied on electricity consumption, typically 5%–15% of the energy charge. It varies by state and consumer category (domestic, commercial, industrial). Delhi charges 5% electricity duty on domestic consumers; Maharashtra charges 16%.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none"><h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">7. Is 5-star AC really better than 3-star for saving electricity?<span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span></h3></summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Yes, significantly. A 5-star 1.5-ton inverter AC typically consumes 1.5–1.6 units per hour; a 3-star fixed-speed equivalent consumes 2.0–2.4 units. Over a summer with 8 hours/day × 150 days, this difference saves 300–500 units — worth ₹1,500–₹3,500 in annual electricity savings.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</CalculatorLayout>

